  "conventions": {
    "citations": "Each territory's source_refs applies to its entire setup row including unit counts and absence of setup markers. PDF pages are one-based; printed_page null means the sheet has no printed page number.",
    "facilities": "Facility records below refer to existing static-map IDs, not additional facility pieces. Count each ID once, even when it serves multiple sea edges. Rail borders are inherited from the map and are not duplicated here.",
    "empty_rows": "An empty units array is a deliberate zero: the complete applicable setup table has no entry for that included land tile. Hainan remains owned by the Kwangtung/Hainan warlord despite no listed starting unit.",
    "construction": "Retained KMT, CCP, warlord and Mongolian setup charts list no construction queues. Japanese national starting queues are specified separately in japan_setup.json.",
    "damage": "No retained unit or facility in these setup rows is marked damaged. Static map assets begin undamaged unless a later explicit scenario override says otherwise.",
    "type_names": "Stable snake-case transcription labels; the static-map label airfield refers to the catalog Airbase (6 IPP), not an unpriced extra type.",
    "minor_wealth": "User-confirmed: controlled/aligned minor assets aggregate into the legally controlling alliance; unaligned uncontrolled warlords count toward no side. This does not grant a minor treasury or collected income.",
    "minor_controller": "Mongolia retains its own national identity under the direct Comintern player, using normal USSR-position movement/recruitment timing. This grants no Soviet participant, possession, treasury or ability."
  },
